## Short version for the thesis

> **Scope and limitations.** The proposed model predicts the evolution of a UAV's physical state over a finite horizon given a known initial state and known control inputs. It is not a standalone navigation system. An IMU alone does not render absolute position or yaw observable, and learned dynamics cannot supply information the sensors do not contain. Open-loop prediction error grows with horizon because of residual model error and because disturbances such as wind are unobserved during imagination. The contribution is to extend the horizon over which prediction remains accurate. In deployment, such a model would serve as the prediction step of a state estimator that receives external position and heading references.

